#:model{:id :brazil-population-aging,
        :as-of "2026-11-22",
        :interpretation
        "2-stock Euler integration (dt 0.05yr x 10yr), dependency-free one-time oracle. Base year is the measured Censo Demográfico 2022 (Segunda Apuração, 2022-08-01): 203,080,756 persons, 22,169,101 aged 65+ (10.9%). Birth/death rates are 2022 Estatísticas do Registro Civil occurred counts; net migration is the 2022 STI saldo (-252,799/yr) from IBGE Projeções Revisão 2024; the aging coefficient is derived from the 2010->2022 census change (midpoint method, elder multiple 3.0 assumed, same as Tier A/B). Year-1 checked for directional/magnitude consistency only (reconciled projection levels sit +3.8% above census and are not matched).",
        :oracle {:script "oracle/brazil_population_oracle_run.cljc (one-time oracle, not CI/gate)",
                 :runtime "basilisp, macOS arm64",
                 :source-edn "examples/brazil-population-aging-scenarios.edn (mirror asserted by grep before run)"},
        :checkpoints-years [0 1 5 10],
        :scenarios
        {
         :baseline-2022-rates {:checkpoints {0 [203.081 22.169] 1 [203.867 22.76] 5 [207.054 25.01] 10 [211.131 27.59] }}
         :lower-fertility {:checkpoints {0 [203.081 22.169] 1 [203.612 22.76] 5 [205.759 24.992] 10 [208.489 27.519] }}
         :faster-aging {:checkpoints {0 [203.081 22.169] 1 [203.867 23.297] 5 [207.054 27.542] 10 [211.131 32.304] }}
         }}
